# What not to upload. Distinct from vercel.json's `excludeFiles`, which trims
# the built function; this trims what leaves the machine in the first place.
#
# tts-cache/sarvam/ is deliberately NOT here. Those 12 clips are the reason a
# deployed instance does not re-synthesise and re-bill every passage on every
# cold start.

# Secrets belong in Vercel's encrypted environment variables, never in the
# uploaded bundle. Baked into a deployment a key cannot be rotated without a
# redeploy, it is readable by anyone who can read the deployment source, and it
# reaches places (build logs, artifacts) nobody audits. sarvam_tts reads .env
# for local convenience only.
.env
.env.*

.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc

# Converted Whisper weights, ~240MB. ASR_BACKEND=sarvam means the deployment
# never loads them, and uploading them would be the slowest part of a deploy.
models/

# IndicF5 clips and their reference prompt: the fallback tier, rebuilt only on
# a machine with a GPU and gated Hugging Face access.
tts-cache/*.wav
tts-prompts/

# Measurement scripts and their fixtures. Kept in the repo because the numbers
# in the code came from them; not needed to serve a request.
test_*.py
eval_*.py
diag_*.py
bench_*.py
dump_*.py
prerender_tts.py
*.md
